<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79745" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παροξ-υντικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for inciting</i> or <i>urging on</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					2.4.29
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι π. πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					20.105
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>exasperating, provoking</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				1.31
			</span></i> : Medic., <i>aggravating</i> bad symptoms, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				1.50
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παροξ-κῶς</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.21a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>easily provoked</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π. τοῦ ἤθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>VV</u>
					1251a8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἡμέρα</span> day <i>of the fit</i>
			in intermittent fevers, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.340
			</span></i>.</div>
